  "issue_title": "dataset: MMLU training silently loads the 2-item toy set (cais/mmlu has no \"train\" split)",
  "issue_body": "### Summary\n\n`python -m trinity.train --benchmark mmlu` trains the coordinator on the **2-item MMLU toy set** instead of the real dataset, silently. Every generation's minibatch is drawn from 2 hand-written questions, so MMLU training is effectively a no-op.\n\n### Root cause\n\n`train.py` loads its tasks with the logical split `\"train\"`:\n\n```python\n# src/trinity/train.py:100\ntasks = load_tasks(args.benchmark, \"train\", max_items=args.max_items, seed=args.seed)\n```\n\n`_load_mmlu_hf` forwards that straight to HuggingFace:\n\n```python\n# src/trinity/orchestration/dataset.py:138\nds = _try_load_hf(\"cais/mmlu\", name=\"all\", split=split or \"test\")   # split == \"train\"\n```\n\nBut **`cais/mmlu` has no split named `train`** \u2014 its splits are `auxiliary_train` (99,842), `dev` (285), `validation` (1,531), and `test` (14,042). `load_dataset(\"cais/mmlu\", \"all\", split=\"train\")` raises, `_try_load_hf` swallows the exception and returns `None`, and `load_tasks` then silently substitutes the built-in toy set:\n\n```python\n# src/trinity/orchestration/dataset.py:514\ntasks = _HF_LOADERS[benchmark](split)\nif not tasks:\n    tasks = _toy_tasks(benchmark)   # <-- 2 MMLU items\n```\n\nSo the load never succeeds for MMLU training *even when `datasets` and the network are fully available*.\n\nThe other benchmarks are unaffected by this specific bug: LiveCodeBench already maps splits to release versions via `_lcb_version_for_split`; GPQA-diamond only has a `train` split (so `\"train\"` works); and math500 falls through to `qwedsacf/competition_math`, which does have a `train` split. MMLU is the one that has a real training split under a *different name* (`auxiliary_train`) and no split-name mapping.\n\n### Impact\n\nAnyone running `--benchmark mmlu` training gets a coordinator \"trained\" on 2 questions with no error, warning, or log line indicating the real dataset was never loaded \u2014 a silent correctness failure of the training entrypoint. (Eval is unaffected: `eval.py` requests `\"test\"`, which is valid.)\n\n### Suggested fix\n\nMap the logical split to a valid MMLU split inside `_load_mmlu_hf`, mirroring the existing `_lcb_version_for_split` pattern \u2014 `\"train\"` -> `auxiliary_train` (MMLU's designated training pool, same row schema as `test`), and pass `test`/`validation`/`dev` through. This makes MMLU training load the real data.\n\nThis is distinct from the (closed, unmerged) #7 \"fail loudly on toy fallback\": that proposes a safeguard when a load fails; this fixes the *reason* the MMLU load fails in the first place. The two are complementary.\n\nHappy to open a PR with the split mapping plus an offline unit test for the mapping helper.",
  "merged_at": "2026-07-11T05:19:25.000Z",
